If a patient has a pain and the patient has a single-joint-osteoarthritis that affects a near-skin-joint and the patient has an insufficient-nonpharmacologic-intervention-response for the pain then it is possible that a topical-NSAID treats the pain.
If a patient has a pain and the patient has a few-joint-osteoarthritis that affects a near-skin-joint and the patient has an insufficient-nonpharmacologic-intervention-response for the pain then it is possible that a topical-NSAID treats the pain.
A near-skin-joint-example is a knee-example.
A nonpharmacologic-intervention-example is an exercise-for-arthritis-pain-example.
